31,2,,status,Benjamin,,ALIVE,"{""seat"":2,""role"":""PARTICIPANT"",""alive"":true}"
32,2,,status,Mizuki,,ALIVE,"{""seat"":3,""role"":""PARTICIPANT"",""alive"":true}"
33,2,,status,Victoria,,ALIVE,"{""seat"":4,""role"":""PARTICIPANT"",""alive"":true}"
34,2,,status,Shunichi,,ALIVE,"{""seat"":5,""role"":""PARTICIPANT"",""alive"":true}"
35,2,1,talk,Mizuki,,"It seems our past successes were tied to accessibility, while our failures were often hidden in the walls of older blocks.","{""words"":21,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
36,2,1,talk,Victoria,,The data suggests a worrying trend. We are paying twice—once for the improvement and once for the temporary space we lose.,"{""words"":21,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
37,2,1,talk,Benjamin,,How predictable. It seems we have a habit of ignoring the clouds until we are already drenched in delays.,"{""words"":19,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
38,2,1,talk,Kenji,,"Guys, the tender records are scary! The costs for mechanical work are way higher than what we usually put in the plans.","{""words"":22,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
39,2,1,talk,Shunichi,,"How shocking. The budget is wrong and the timing is off. Now, shall we discuss the people actually breaking their backs?","{""words"":21,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
40,2,2,talk,Mizuki,,"@Shunichi, the human element is key. If the staff are overburdened, a fancy new facility won't help if they can't maintain it.","{""words"":22,""mentions"":[""Shunichi""],""raw_differs"":false}"
41,2,2,talk,Victoria,,"@Mizuki, that's true, but we must also consider the students. The timetable losses are a hidden tax on our education quality.","{""words"":21,""mentions"":[""Mizuki""],""raw_differs"":false}"
42,2,2,talk,Benjamin,,"@Victoria, a ""hidden tax"" indeed. I wonder if we are simply squeezing a year's worth of work into a few weeks of panic.","{""words"":23,""mentions"":[""Victoria""],""raw_differs"":false}"
43,2,2,talk,Kenji,,"@Benjamin, that's exactly it! We plan for a dream price, but the market gives us a nightmare. We need a plan that's realistic.","{""words"":23,""mentions"":[""Benjamin""],""raw_differs"":false}"
44,2,2,talk,Shunichi,,"@Kenji, ""realistic"" usually means ""cheaper"" in your vocabulary. I'm talking about the technicians doing manual labor because the gear is obsolete.","{""words"":21,""mentions"":[""Kenji""],""raw_differs"":false}"
45,2,3,talk,Mizuki,,We need a project that balances accessibility for all with a realistic understanding of the building's age and the staff's capacity.,"{""words"":21,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
46,2,3,talk,Victoria,,I am concerned that we will choose a plan that looks good on paper but disrupts the timetable beyond recovery.,"{""words"":20,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
47,2,3,talk,Benjamin,,"I suggest we avoid any plan that relies on ""optimistic"" weather windows or complex, unpriced mechanical upgrades.","{""words"":17,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
48,2,3,talk,Kenji,,"I agree with Benjamin! Let's pick something where the costs are stable and the benefits are clear to everyone, not just one department.","{""words"":23,""mentions"":[""Benjamin""],""raw_differs"":false}"
49,2,3,talk,Shunichi,,"If we pick a plan that adds more ""features"" without adding staff, we're just rewarding the exhausted with more work.","{""words"":20,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
