60,3,1,talk,Mizuki,,"Option A is tempting because it's accessible, but the ""ground-floor"" part makes me worry about the hidden hazards I found.","{""words"":20,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
61,3,1,talk,Victoria,,"Option B is interesting, but we must ask: how many rooms will be out of service during the fit-out, and who benefits most?","{""words"":23,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
62,3,1,talk,Benjamin,,Option C is a delightful trap. It's entirely exposed to the weather—the very thing that has historically devoured our schedules.,"{""words"":20,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
63,3,1,talk,Kenji,,Option D sounds like a nightmare! Mechanical and ventilation work is exactly where the tender prices are skyrocketing right now.,"{""words"":20,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
64,3,1,talk,Shunichi,,"@Kenji, for once we agree on the cost, but you're missing the point. Option D is the only one that stops the staff from doing manual labor.","{""words"":27,""mentions"":[""Kenji""],""raw_differs"":false}"
65,3,2,talk,Mizuki,,"@Shunichi, I understand the need, but if Option D causes massive delays due to the building's age, the staff will suffer more.","{""words"":22,""mentions"":[""Shunichi""],""raw_differs"":false}"
66,3,2,talk,Victoria,,"I'm leaning toward Option B. It's a specialized facility, but if it's open to all campus users, it maximizes the post-occupancy value.","{""words"":22,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
67,3,2,talk,Benjamin,,"@Victoria, provided the ""fit-out"" doesn't involve moving walls that weren't meant to be moved. Option A seems the most... contained.","{""words"":20,""mentions"":[""Victoria""],""raw_differs"":false}"
68,3,2,talk,Kenji,,"Option A is great! It's mostly furniture and power. The costs are stable, and it's a win for everyone, not just one lab.","{""words"":23,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
69,3,2,talk,Shunichi,,"@Kenji, ""a win for everyone"" is a lovely phrase for ""doing nothing that actually fixes a systemic problem."" Option D is a necessity.","{""words"":23,""mentions"":[""Kenji""],""raw_differs"":false}"
70,3,3,talk,Mizuki,,"I cannot ignore the staff's struggle, but I also cannot ignore the risk of a failed project. Option B is a balanced compromise.","{""words"":23,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
71,3,3,talk,Victoria,,"If we choose B, we must ensure the booking system is integrated into the timetable from day one to avoid the losses I saw.","{""words"":24,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
72,3,3,talk,Benjamin,,"I find Option A the most rational. It avoids the weather of C, the price volatility of D, and the complexity of B.","{""words"":23,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
73,3,3,talk,Kenji,,I'm with Benjamin! Option A is the safest bet for the budget and the most helpful for the students. Let's go with A!,"{""words"":23,""mentions"":[""Benjamin""],""raw_differs"":false}"
74,3,3,talk,Shunichi,,"Safe bets are for people who don't have to maintain the equipment. I'll stand by D. It's the only choice that isn't just ""window dressing.""","{""words"":25,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
75,3,4,talk,Mizuki,,"I'll consider the balance. While D is necessary, B provides a new, shared resource that avoids the ground-floor risks of A.","{""words"":21,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
76,3,4,talk,Victoria,,"I will vote for B. It addresses the need for shared, high-utility space while being less disruptive than a full lab overhaul.","{""words"":22,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
77,3,4,talk,Benjamin,,I shall remain with A. It is the only option that doesn't invite a calendar slip of epic proportions.,"{""words"":19,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
78,3,4,talk,Kenji,,I'm sticking with A! It's the most positive change we can make without risking a budget disaster.,"{""words"":17,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
79,3,4,talk,Shunichi,,"I've heard enough. I'll vote for D. If you'd rather have a ""study commons"" than working labs, that's your lack of vision.","{""words"":22,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
